{"name":"Sandpaper","hex":"#d7b1a5","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sandpaper","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Strong paper coated with (traditionally) sand or (today) manufactured aluminum oxide, silicon carbide, or other abrasive material, used for smoothing and polishing.","A sheet of such paper."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To polish or grind (a surface) with or as if with sandpaper."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sandpaper"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sandpaper","blocks":[{"text":"Sandpaper, also known as coated abrasive or emery paper, is a type of material that consists of sheets of paper or cloth with an abrasive substance (grit) glued to one face."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Schleifpapier_verschiedene_Sorten.jpg/330px-Schleifpapier_verschiedene_Sorten.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sandpaper","wikidata":"Q142274"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/SCSandpaper.jpg/500px-SCSandpaper.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/SCSandpaper.jpg/1280px-SCSandpaper.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/SCSandpaper.jpg/500px-SCSandpaper.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"320 grit silicon carbide sandpaper, with close-up view","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASCSandpaper.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Liivapaber-karedusindeksid.jpg/500px-Liivapaber-karedusindeksid.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Liivapaber-karedusindeksid.jpg/500px-Liivapaber-kared